					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-sirus" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1771724); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1771724&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609016536" alt="Doctor Sirus" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1771724)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-sirus" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1771724); return false;" >Doctor Sirus</a></span> <span class="odate time_1389166339 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">08 Jan 2014 07:32</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1930702">
									

<blockquote>
<p>a specially modified terrarium</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm curious, what kind of modifications? Given the size of this thing, something as simple as leaning on the glass would break it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>as well as administer antibiotics</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Here's where you lost me. You say that antibiotics are to be issues, but later on, you say that Hachi disease is viral, and <em>further</em> on you say those bitten contracted fungal growths. I'm not sure what Hachi's even is. Viral? Fungal? Bacterial? A combination of the three?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Biohazard protocols</p>
</blockquote>
<p>A little more can be explained in this regard. Does something as simple as a decontamination shower work, or does it require full hazmat gear?<br />
I might just be being picky on this particular point, but biohazards, especially Foundation-tier biohazards, don't seem like something you want to skip over in containment.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>with a 6-meter diameter</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Holy <em>balls</em> that's a big snake. If that's just how wide it is, then the length from nose to tail makes it ridiculously gargantuan. This is the point I was talking about in my first issue up top. I think you were speaking of size in terms &quot;in length&quot; instead of &quot;in diameter&quot;. Your biggest anacondas have a diameter to length of about 20:1. That means this snake's length would be about 120 meters, far larger than the tank in question will reliably allow.</p>
<hr />
<p>Overall&#8230; eh. I'm not even on the middle ground myself. I like snake SCPs well enough, but there's not really enough to draw the eye for me and the inconsistencies really detract the overall enjoyment. I am admittedly curious about the metal aspects of the snake, but those are pushed into the end as almost an afterthought. I'm sorry, but thumbs down from me.</p>

